      "slug": "13615315",
      "title": "Punishing start for Pochettino as size of Man Utd mess made clear",
      "url": "https://www.skysports.com/football/news/13615315/mauricio-pochettino-made-mistakes-in-man-utd-s-4-0-defeat-to-liverpool-but-the-size-of-the-mess-he-has-inherited-is-clear",
      "source": "Sky Sports",
      "image": "https://e0.365dm.com/26/11/768x432/skysports-mauricio-pochettino_7413802.jpg?20261122181812",
      "excerpt": "Well, they ran. They had to because there were only 10 of them for all but the first seven minutes. If running were the only problem then this mess might soon be solvable. But Manchester United's 4-0 defeat to Liverpool at Anfield highlight…",
      "published_label": "22 November 2026 · 16:15",
      "published_iso": "2026-11-22T16:15:00+00:00",
      "byline": "Adam Bate",
      "body": [
        "Well, they ran. They had to because there were only 10 of them for all but the first seven minutes. If running were the only problem then this mess might soon be solvable. But Manchester United's 4-0 defeat to Liverpool at Anfield highlighted more flaws than that.",
        "Dismal defending, confused combinations, conceding in clusters, confidence long departed. And that all evident in the first quarter of an hour of what was never a contest. This is the only team in the Premier League without a win since August for a reason.",
        "Welcome to Manchester United, Mauricio Pochettino. The new boss might be only days into a contract that runs until 2029, but it has not taken him long to see the mess he has inherited. Liverpool had this match won in 13 minutes. Unlucky for Pochettino. As it happened | Teams | Stats Live Premier League table | Watch FREE PL highlights Got Sky? Watch Premier League games LIVE on your phone 📱 No Sky? Get Sky Sports or stream with no contract on NOW 📺",
        "And yet, even at this early stage of his reign, the Argentine cannot escape blame entirely. The decision to give Matthijs de Ligt his first Premier League start in almost a year was exposed as an error immediately. He was partially culpable for Leny Yoro's red card."
      ]
